# SYNOPSIS

```c
#include <vxui.h>

vx_app *vx_app_open(const char *id);
const char *vx_app_error(const vx_app *app);
bool vx_wait(vx_app *app, vx_event *ev, vx_instant deadline);

vx_window *vx_window_open(vx_app *app, const char *title,
                          uint32_t width, uint32_t height);
void vx_window_redraw(vx_window *win);
void vx_window_animate(vx_window *win, bool on);
void vx_window_title(vx_window *win, const char *title);

vx_canvas *vx_canvas_begin(vx_window *win, const vx_frame_event *frame);
void vx_clear(vx_canvas *c, vx_color colour);
void vx_fill_rect(vx_canvas *c, float x, float y, float w, float h,
                  vx_color colour);
void vx_circle(vx_canvas *c, float x, float y, float r, vx_color colour);
void vx_canvas_present(vx_canvas *c);

vx_pixels vx_pixels_begin(vx_window *win, const vx_frame_event *frame);
void vx_pixels_present(vx_window *win, vx_pixels *px);

vx_voice *vx_voice_open(vx_app *app, vx_sound sound);
void vx_voice_play(vx_voice *voice);
```

# DESCRIPTION

vxui is the app tier (03 §6), v0 (M7 step 7e2).
An app has one loop and one wait, its own: `vx_wait` returns the next event of any of its windows in libvx's `vx_event` (loop(2)), with vxui's kinds, the window as `source`: `VX_FRAME` (`frame`: its sequence, `target`, `prev_presented` and `dt`), `VX_KEY` (`keyboard`: the HID usage, its unmodified rune, the modifiers, down and repeat), `VX_POINTER` (`pointer`: x and y in the window, the buttons, the wheel), `VX_TEXT` (`text`), `VX_CONFIGURE` (`configure`: the size, focus) and `VX_CLOSE`.
With a deadline that comes first, it returns `true` and `VX_NONE`.
The toolkit never calls back.

A window is made by opening `/wsys/new`, the window server's app attach (winsrv(8); a manifest gives it with `mount=/wsys srv=wsys aname=self`), titled and sized with its `ctl`, and drawn into two buffers in turn.
It draws only when asked: `vx_window_redraw` asks for one `VX_FRAME`, `vx_window_animate` for one every frame the output shows; either comes only with a credit of the frame protocol in hand, so an idle window costs nothing.

`vx_canvas_begin` and `vx_canvas_present` bracket drawing with `vx_clear`, `vx_fill_rect` and `vx_circle` (antialiased); colours are XRGB or the theme's (`VX_THEME_BG`, `VX_THEME_FG`, `VX_THEME_ACCENT`, `VX_THEME_FACE`).
`vx_pixels_begin` gives the buffer itself (`data`, `w`, `h`, `stride`) and its `age`, the presents since its contents were last shown (0 for a new one); `vx_pixels_present` presents it.

Errors are sticky: a failed open makes the next `vx_wait` return `false`, and `vx_app_error` says why, so a program need not check each call.

Voices are numbered now and sound with audiod (M13): `vx_voice_open` gives one, `vx_voice_play` is silent until then.

